WEBVTT

00:00:08.411 --> 00:00:11.864
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> One invention that definitely improved the lives of millions of people

00:00:12.081 --> 00:00:13.582
was the disposable nappy.

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.331
They were invented by a woman called Marion Donovan.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:27.091
And now another invention which has made life easier.

00:00:29.044 --> 00:00:32.635
The dishwasher was invented by a woman called Josephine Cochrane.

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:40.519
The car was invented by a man, but it was a woman, Mary Anderson,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.174
who solved one of the biggest problems of driving.

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:49.139
On a trip to New York in 1903 Anderson noticed

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.592
that drivers had to open their windows

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.994
to see where they were going when it was raining.

00:00:59.152 --> 00:01:03.752
Our fourth invention made life safer for people living in flats or apartments –

00:01:04.376 --> 00:01:06.322
video entry phones.

00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:13.669
They were invented in 1966 by Marie Van Brittan Brown.

00:01:22.376 --> 00:01:25.363
And now an invention that has saved a lot of lives.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:30.514
The modern life raft was invented by Maria Beasley in 1880.

00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:43.289
Our last invention is one of today’s most important green technologies.

00:01:46.452 --> 00:01:50.246
Mária Telkes, a Hungarian-American scientist, worked at the

00:01:50.247 --> 00:01:54.919
Massachusetts Institute of Technology in the United States in the 1940s.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.979
She was so interested in the power of the sun that her nickname was ‘the Sun Queen’.